ROUTE HOSTING (web /gas-price)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The web page is the standalone route `/gas-price` (web App.tsx L454), surfaced in the
"Integrations" side-nav group (Layout.tsx L397: label "Gas Prices", fuel icon). The native
shell has no "Integrations" route group, so — exactly like the sibling `TeslaOrders`
(also a features/admin page that the web places in a non-System group) — a new top-level
`AppRoute.gasPrice` is added and mapped to the native `.account` group, alongside Settings
/ Active Orders, where the EIA gas-price integration (formerly a `/settings#gas-price`
section) belongs. `AppRoute.gasPrice` carries pathSegment "gas-price" (→ path "/gas-price"),
SF Symbol `fuelpump.fill`, group `.account`. `AppRouteParser` keys on the first path segment,
so no alias is needed; `/gas-price` (+ trailing slash + `teslasync://gas-price`) resolves to
`.gasPrice`. `GasPriceAutoPollRouteRegistration` hosts the page on `.gasPrice` and is chained
into `\.routeHosts` in TeslaSyncApp.swift, so it is reachable via the Account-group sidebar
entry and any `/gas-price` deep link.

